WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:43.240
Open the branch selector. Choose the branch that contains the prepared Training Echo module.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:54.354
This is the original training branch. These prepared files are the starting point for the release.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:01:10.479
Open modules, then training_echo. Each module has its own folder.

00:01:10.479 --> 00:01:18.482
The folder contains the manifest, implementation, dependencies, fixture and output assertion.

00:01:18.482 --> 00:01:26.563
From the module folder, open manifest.yaml.

00:01:26.563 --> 00:02:02.055
The manifest declares the input, output and runtime. This prepared version starts disabled and hidden.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:10.057
From the module folder, open run.py.

00:02:10.057 --> 00:02:45.773
run.py reads the input text and writes training_echo.csv with the text and its character count.

00:02:45.773 --> 00:02:53.770
From the module folder, open requirements.txt.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:03:10.668
requirements.txt is empty: this training module uses only the Python standard library.

00:03:10.668 --> 00:03:18.703
From the module folder, open validation.json.

00:03:18.703 --> 00:03:35.628
validation.json supplies a known input and an invalid case for local acceptance.

00:03:35.628 --> 00:03:43.635
From the module folder, open assert_output.py.

00:03:43.635 --> 00:04:19.324
assert_output.py checks the actual CSV contents, including escaping and the character count.

00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:32.300
Return to the module folder. Next, validate these files before reviewing the pull request.

00:04:32.333 --> 00:04:48.456
Start in the training branch. Backend access rules live outside the module folder.

00:04:48.456 --> 00:05:03.695
Open supabase, then functions, then _shared.

00:05:03.695 --> 00:05:13.772
Open module-entitlements.ts to find the module-to-tier policy.

00:05:13.772 --> 00:05:37.876
In MODULE_ACCESS, set training_echo to "silver" alongside the new module files in the initial PR.

00:05:37.876 --> 00:05:52.733
The release owner deploys this Silver policy once after merge. Later manifest maintenance uses merges.

00:05:52.733 --> 00:06:08.000
Run the module acceptance command against the prepared files.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:23.267
A passing result checks the output CSV contents, escaping and character count.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:53.407
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

00:06:53.407 --> 00:07:05.636
Open PR #54. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

00:07:05.636 --> 00:08:01.225
Review the module implementation, manifest and acceptance files before release.

00:08:01.225 --> 00:08:30.126
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

00:08:30.126 --> 00:09:07.119
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

00:09:07.119 --> 00:09:20.067
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:41.090
Open Checks, then expand module-ci to see its individual jobs.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:50.972
Select validate to open the recorded job and its conclusion.

00:09:50.972 --> 00:10:23.067
Inspect the validation result and its logged steps for this exact PR head.

00:10:23.067 --> 00:10:40.700
Original recording: review the passing checks, then merge the prepared module PR.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:58.333
The initial released manifest is disabled and hidden.

00:10:58.333 --> 00:11:05.567
Original registry readback: locate the released module and inspect its flags.

00:11:05.567 --> 00:11:12.800
Both Training Echo and Coptis are held disabled and hidden here.

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:19.800
Recorded command output: the release owner manually deploys submit-job with the reviewed Silver policy.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:26.800
This is the one-time backend setup for this walkthrough. The following maintenance edits use manifest PRs.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:56.934
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

00:11:56.934 --> 00:12:08.954
Open PR #56. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

00:12:08.954 --> 00:12:33.919
enabled allows new jobs. ui.visible controls whether the catalog offers the module.

00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:50.852
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

00:12:50.852 --> 00:13:27.910
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:41.000
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:49.300
Original recorded change: enable the module and make it visible through PR #56.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:57.600
The reviewed manifest is now ready for its registry release.

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:19.100
Original recording: merge PR #56 after its checks pass.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:40.600
Verify that the registry workflow checked out the intended merge commit.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:15:06.733
From the repository, open Actions to inspect the automatic registry release.

00:15:06.733 --> 00:15:19.834
Choose the run for the intended merge. Its commit must match the change you meant to release.

00:15:19.834 --> 00:15:49.700
This completed run projects the manifest into the registry. It does not deploy frontend or function code.

00:15:49.733 --> 00:15:56.733
Original Silver test: Training Echo is enabled and visible in the catalog.

00:15:56.733 --> 00:16:02.733
Enter the test text and select Run. The following submission is the original recorded action.

00:16:02.733 --> 00:16:24.733
The accepted job is queued and executed. Wait for its status to change.

00:16:24.733 --> 00:16:29.733
The job has succeeded and its result is available.

00:16:29.733 --> 00:16:41.600
The verified private CSV contains the exact input text and its character count.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:53.600
The module writes this local file on the runner. The manifest tells the runner which file to collect and which MIME type to send.

00:16:53.600 --> 00:17:05.600
The path names the local output. Its basename becomes the stored filename; text/csv describes the file type. It does not convert the contents.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:17.600
The runner sends the file bytes to job-callback. The callback chooses the bucket and creates a unique folder for this job and upload attempt.

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:29.600
The bucket is fixed in backend code, not the manifest. Storage path: job-results/<job-id>/<attempt-id>/training_echo.csv.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:41.600
The CSV is a private file object in Supabase Storage. The job row holds its reference; the CSV contents are not imported into database rows.

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:53.600
The Vault requests the result. get-result checks membership and returns a download link valid for 60 seconds. Coptis uses the same path pattern with docking_results.csv.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:45.973
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

00:18:45.973 --> 00:18:57.981
Open PR #57. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

00:18:57.981 --> 00:19:22.973
This PR changes the title, description and visibility together. Hiding also removes the updated catalog card.

00:19:22.973 --> 00:19:39.913
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

00:19:39.913 --> 00:20:17.012
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

00:20:17.012 --> 00:20:30.100
To see a new name and description in the catalog, keep enabled and ui.visible true when releasing those edits.

00:20:30.133 --> 00:20:38.100
Original recorded change: update the title and description, then hide catalog discovery.

00:20:38.100 --> 00:20:46.067
These manifest fields are released through PR #57.

00:20:46.067 --> 00:21:08.233
Original recording: merge PR #57 and verify its registry release.

00:21:08.233 --> 00:21:30.400
Wait for release-modules to succeed, then refresh the Vault. Manifest-only maintenance needs no function deployment.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:40.400
Original readback: the module is no longer offered in the catalog.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:50.400
This verifies hiding, not the new catalog text. Existing jobs and results remain available in Runs.

00:21:50.400 --> 00:22:20.459
From the repository, open Pull requests. The completed demonstration PRs are in Closed.

00:22:20.459 --> 00:22:32.515
Open PR #59. Read the description and source branch, then inspect the changed files.

00:22:32.515 --> 00:22:57.608
Set enabled to false to stop new jobs, and ui.visible to false to hide catalog discovery.

00:22:57.608 --> 00:23:14.479
Read the changed lines, then return to the conversation to inspect checks and the merge record.

00:23:14.479 --> 00:23:51.415
Inspect the completed checks for this PR before relying on the merge.

00:23:51.415 --> 00:24:04.300
Next, watch the recorded release and verify that its outcome matches this reviewed change.

00:24:04.333 --> 00:24:13.300
Original recorded change: disable the module and hide it through PR #59.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:22.267
Disabling stops new jobs; hiding removes catalog discovery.

00:24:22.267 --> 00:24:44.467
Original recording: verify the final registry release after PR #59.

00:24:44.467 --> 00:25:06.667
Training Echo and Coptis are both disabled and hidden.

00:25:06.667 --> 00:25:23.809
Recorded after cleanup: open the catalog and retained results. The account has been restored to Platinum.

00:25:23.809 --> 00:25:37.851
Open Skill Catalog from the sidebar. Training Echo is hidden after the final disable.

00:25:37.851 --> 00:25:56.837
The catalog contains the currently available skills. Historical results remain in Runs.

00:25:56.837 --> 00:26:10.977
Click Runs. The successful training_echo entry from the Silver test is still retained.

00:26:10.977 --> 00:26:22.913
Open VISUALIZE on that run to inspect its saved output.

00:26:22.913 --> 00:26:37.910
Table shows the original test input and its character count: 36.

00:26:37.910 --> 00:26:52.882
Raw exposes the saved CSV. This is the original result, not a new module run.

00:26:52.882 --> 00:27:06.767
Close returns to Runs. The disabled and hidden module retains this earlier Silver test result.
